#: distances.cpp:18
msgid ""
"A meter is equivalent to roughly 1/10,000,000th the distance between the "
"equator and the North Pole, passing through Lyons, France.  A meter was "
"redefined as 1650763.73 times the wavelength of light emitted from "
"krypton-86.  1982 saw another update: A meter is now 1/299,692,458th the "
"distance light travels in a vacuum, in one second."
msgstr ""
"'n meter is dieselfde as na rofweg 1/10,000,000th die afstand tussen die "
"ewenaar en die Noord Pool, aangee deur Lyons, Frankryk.  'n meter was "
"herdefinieër as 1650763.73  times  die golflengte van ligte uitgestuur van "
"krypton-86.  1982 saag nog 'n dateer op: 'n meter is nou 1/299,692,458th die "
"afstand ligte trek in 'n vakuum, in een tweede."

#: distances.cpp:20
msgid "The 'A' is an 'A' with a small circle above.  It is commonly used in Swedish."
msgstr ""
"Die ''n' is 'n ''n' met 'n klein sirkel boonste.  Dit is algemeen gebruik "
"word in Sweedse."

#: distances.cpp:24
msgid ""
"A lightyear is the distance light travels in a year.  The speed of light is "
"299,792,458 meters/second or 186,000 miles/second."
msgstr ""
"'n ligjaar is die afstand ligte trek in 'n jaar.  die spoed van ligte is "
"299,792,458 meters/tweede of 186,000 myle/tweede."

#: distances.cpp:26
msgid "An astronomical unit is the mean distance between the Earth and the Sun."
msgstr "'n astronomiese eenheid is die beteken afstand tussen die Aarde en die Sun."

#: distances.cpp:27
msgid ""
"A nautical mile is often used at sea, defined as one minute of the mean "
"latitude on earth.  This makes perfect sense at sea, where it's possible to "
"measure latitude, but not distance."
msgstr ""
"'n see myl is gereeld gebruik word na see, gedefinieër as een minuut van "
"die beteken lengtegraad op aarde.  Hierdie maak perfek sin na see, waar dit "
"is moontlik na meet lengtegraad, maar nie afstand."

#: distances.cpp:28
msgid ""
"Also known as the statute mile.  This word comes from the latin phrase "
"\"millia passuum\", or \"thousand paces\"-- the distance a Roman legion "
"could travel in a thousand paces (two steps)."
msgstr ""
"Asook bekend as die statute myl.  Hierdie woord kom van die latyn frase "
"\"millia passuum\", of \"duisend tree\"-- die afstand 'n Roman soldaat kon "
"reis in 'n duisend tree (twee stappe)."

